James inquired about how to describe proposed edits in Markdown, specifically for deletions and insertions. I suggested using strikethrough for deletions with double tildes (`~~`), and bold or italic formatting for insertions using asterisks or underscores. I provided an example where "brown" is marked for deletion while "red" and "but energetic" are proposed insertions. To enhance track changes, I recommended tools or editors that support Markdown extensions and visual diff features.
